2. Identify the Models: For each service you listed, identify its service model (IaaS / PaaS / SaaS) and deployment model (Public / Private / Hybrid / Community). Briefly explain why you chose that classification.
-Messenger is classified as Software as a Service (SaaS) because it provides messaging and communication services through the internet without requiring users to manage any hardware or software. Its deployment model is 
Public Cloud because it is available to anyone with a Meta account.

-Facebook is also a Software as a Service (SaaS) application because it delivers social networking features directly through a web browser or mobile app. Its deployment model is Public Cloud since it is accessible to 
millions of users worldwide over the internet.

-Google Chrome can also be considered Software as a Service (SaaS) in the context of its cloud-based features, such as syncing bookmarks, passwords, extensions, and browsing history through a Google account. 
Its deployment model is Public Cloud because these cloud services are available to any user with internet access and a Google account.

3. Git & GitHub for Cloud Projects: Explain why version control is critical when working with cloud infrastructure. How does GitHub help teams collaborate, track changes, and prevent errors when managing cloud resources?
- Version control is critical when working with cloud infrastructure because configuration files, application code, and deployment scripts are updated regularly. Without version control, it is easy to lose previous work, 
overwrite changes, or introduce errors that are difficult to fix. Git records every change made to a project, making it possible to review history or restore earlier versions when needed. GitHub further improves teamwork 
by providing a central repository where developers can collaborate using branches, pull requests, code reviews, and commit history. These features help teams track changes, prevent conflicts, reduce errors, and ensure that 
cloud resources are managed in a reliable and organized manner.
